Claim 09 - Manual test recommendations with criticality / risk score
=====================================================================

Method: Static inspection only. No CLI / live tests executed.

Findings:

1. A dedicated module generates manual-test suggestions:
   - src/goal/manual-tests.ts:8-62 (MANUAL_TESTS_SYSTEM_PROMPT explicitly
     instructs the model to emit `criticality` integers 1..10 with reasons)
   - src/goal/manual-tests.ts:168-172 (clampCriticality clamps to 1..10
     and defaults to 5)
   - src/goal/manual-tests.ts:224-226 (fallbackCriticality assigns a
     decaying value 3..6 when the model returns fewer suggestions than
     requested)
   - src/goal/manual-tests.ts:327-399 (generateManualTests, the public
     entry point; filters to done steps, parses, normalizes, and returns
     ManualTestSuggestion[])

2. The data type is part of the goal contract, not ad hoc:
   - src/goal/types.ts:123-125 (`export type ManualTestSuggestion = {
     description: string; criticality: number; reason?: string;
     detail: string; };`)

3. Manual tests are invoked at goal completion, not as roadmap aspiration:
   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:52 (`import { generateManualTests }
     from "./manual-tests.js";`)
   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:1036-1048 (when the goal reaches the
     all-done path, generateManualTests is awaited; failure is
     fail-open and recorded as manualTestsError)
   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:1061-1069 (the `all_done` status event
     carries `manualTests` and `manualTestsError` to the channel layer)

4. The Telegram channel renders criticality to the operator:
   - src/telegram/goal-formatting.ts:96 (renders each suggestion as
     `**Test N: <desc> [N/10 Critical]**`)
   - src/telegram/goal-sending.ts:275-288 (persistManualTests writes
     suggestions and any generation error onto the run record so the
     summary survives restart)

Implementation summary:
- After every completed goal the system asks the model to enumerate
  manual verification steps that the automated harness cannot perform
  (real Telegram, UI, multi-service integration, devices).
- Each suggestion carries a 1..10 criticality value, a reason, and
  human-friendly numbered steps.
- The suggestions are surfaced in the goal summary alongside the
  artifact trail; failures to generate them are non-blocking and shown
  to the operator as a notice rather than swallowed.

Safe README wording:
- "After a goal completes, SmithersBot suggests manual verification
  steps the bot could not perform itself, each tagged with a 1..10
  criticality rating."

Unsafe wording to avoid:
- "SmithersBot runs manual tests for you" (it suggests, it does not run).
- "Risk score" framed as a quantitative safety/compliance metric -
  criticality here is an LLM-assigned heuristic for operator
  prioritization, not a calibrated risk model.

STATUS: verified
REASON: Manual-test generation with a 1..10 criticality field is fully
implemented, wired into the all-done path of agent-executor.ts, typed
in the goal contract, persisted on the run, and rendered to the
operator in the Telegram channel.
